## MCP TOOL REFERENCE — PHASE 1 (27 TOOLS)

### Collections (5 tools)

#### qdrant_list_collections
  Description: List all collections in the Qdrant instance
  Args: {} (none)
  API: GET /collections
  Returns: [{name: str, status: str}]
  Use first: always list before operating on collections you don't know exist

#### qdrant_get_collection
  Description: Get detailed info about a collection — config, stats, schema
  Args: {collection_name: str}
  API: GET /collections/{collection_name}
  Returns:
    {
      vectors_count: int,           // total vectors stored
      indexed_vectors_count: int,   // vectors in HNSW index
      points_count: int,            // total points (may differ from vectors_count for named vectors)
      segments_count: int,
      config: {
        params: {
          vectors: {size: int, distance: str, on_disk: bool},
          shard_number: int,
          replication_factor: int
        },
        optimizer_config: {...},
        wal_config: {...}
      },
      payload_schema: {field_name: {data_type: str, indexed: bool}}
    }
  ⚠ indexed_vectors_count < vectors_count = indexing in progress (HNSW building)

#### qdrant_create_collection
  Description: Create a new vector collection
  Args:
    collection_name: str
    vector_size: int          — embedding dimensions (1536=OpenAI, 768=sentence-transformers,
                                 1024=Voyage AI text-embedding-3)
    distance: str             — "Cosine" | "Euclid" | "Dot" | "Manhattan"
    on_disk: bool (optional)  — store vectors on disk (saves RAM for large collections)
    shard_number: int (opt)   — number of shards (default 1 for single-node)
    replication_factor: int (opt) — replication factor (default 1)
  API: PUT /collections/{collection_name}
  Body: {"vectors": {"size": int, "distance": str, ...}}
  Returns: {"status": "created", "collection": name, "response": {...}}
  ⚠ Distance metric CANNOT be changed after creation — choose carefully
  Convention: Cosine for text embeddings (most common), Euclid for geometric data

#### qdrant_delete_collection
  Description: Delete a collection and all its data — PERMANENT, IRREVERSIBLE
  Args: {collection_name: str}
  API: DELETE /collections/{collection_name}
  Returns: {"status": "deleted"}
  ⚠ DESTRUCTIVE — always confirm before calling. No undo. Consider snapshot first.
  Annotation: destructiveHint: True

#### qdrant_update_collection
  Description: Update collection optimizer config or other mutable parameters
  Args:
    collection_name: str
    optimizers_config: dict (optional) — e.g. {"indexing_threshold": 20000}
    params: dict (optional)            — e.g. {"replication_factor": 2}
  API: PATCH /collections/{collection_name}
  Use for: adjusting indexing thresholds, enabling on-disk storage, tuning for workload

