### Points (6 tools)

#### qdrant_upsert_points
  Description: Insert or update points — idempotent by point ID
  Args:
    collection_name: str
    points: list[dict]   — each point: {id: int|str, vector: [float,...], payload: dict}
    wait: bool (default True) — wait for indexing confirmation
  API: PUT /collections/{collection_name}/points
  Body: {"points": [...]}
  Point schema:
    id: integer or UUID string — must be unique within collection
    vector: list of floats — must match collection's vector_size exactly
    payload: dict — arbitrary JSON, filterable via payload indexes
  Returns: {"operation_id": int, "status": "completed"}
  Idempotent: re-upserting same ID overwrites the point

#### qdrant_get_points
  Description: Retrieve points by explicit IDs
  Args:
    collection_name: str
    ids: list[int|str]
    with_payload: bool (default True)
    with_vectors: bool (default False)   — omit for bandwidth efficiency
  API: POST /collections/{collection_name}/points
  Body: {"ids": [...], "with_payload": true, "with_vectors": false}
  Returns: list of {id, payload, vector?}

#### qdrant_delete_points
  Description: Delete points by IDs or filter — PERMANENT
  Args:
    collection_name: str
    ids: list (optional)         — delete specific IDs
    filter: dict (optional)      — delete by payload filter (see filter syntax below)
    wait: bool (default True)
  API: POST /collections/{collection_name}/points/delete
  ⚠ DESTRUCTIVE — filter-based delete can remove large batches. Confirm scope first.
  Annotation: destructiveHint: True

#### qdrant_scroll_points
  Description: Paginate through all points in a collection with optional filter
  Args:
    collection_name: str
    filter: dict (optional)
    limit: int (default 10, max 1000)
    offset: int|str (optional)     — point ID to start after (cursor-based pagination)
    with_payload: bool (default True)
    with_vectors: bool (default False)
  API: POST /collections/{collection_name}/points/scroll
  Returns: {points: [...], next_page_offset: int|str|null}
  Use next_page_offset as offset in next call. null = last page.

#### qdrant_set_payload
  Description: Update payload fields on existing points without replacing vectors
  Args:
    collection_name: str
    payload: dict            — fields to set/update (merged, not replaced)
    ids: list (optional)     — target specific IDs
    filter: dict (optional)  — target by filter
    wait: bool (default True)
  API: POST /collections/{collection_name}/points/payload
  Use for: updating metadata, adding tags, changing status fields on stored vectors

#### qdrant_count_points
  Description: Count points in a collection, optionally filtered
  Args:
    collection_name: str
    filter: dict (optional)   — count only matching points
    exact: bool (default True) — exact count (slower) vs estimate (faster)
  API: POST /collections/{collection_name}/points/count
  Returns: {"count": int}

