### Aliases (3 tools)

  Aliases enable zero-downtime collection swaps. Build new collection alongside old,
  then atomically move the alias. Clients reference the alias, never the raw name.

#### qdrant_list_aliases
  Description: List all collection aliases
  Args: {} (none)
  API: GET /aliases
  Returns: [{alias_name, collection_name}]

#### qdrant_create_alias
  Description: Create or update an alias pointing to a collection
  Args:
    alias_name: str         — the name clients will use
    collection_name: str    — the underlying collection
  API: POST /collections/aliases
  Body: {"actions": [{"create_alias": {"alias_name": ..., "collection_name": ...}}]}
  Pattern for zero-downtime swap:
    1. Build new collection: aiana_memories_v2
    2. Backfill vectors into new collection
    3. qdrant_create_alias {alias_name: "aiana_memories", collection_name: "aiana_memories_v2"}
    4. Old collection aiana_memories_v1 can now be safely deleted

#### qdrant_delete_alias
  Description: Remove an alias
  Args: {alias_name: str}
  API: POST /collections/aliases
  Body: {"actions": [{"delete_alias": {"alias_name": ...}}]}

