## QDRANT FILTER SYNTAX

Filters are used in scroll, delete, count, search, and query_points.
They operate on payload fields.

### Common filter patterns

#### Match exact value (keyword field)
  {"must": [{"key": "project", "match": {"value": "git-steer"}}]}

#### Match any of (array contains)
  {"must": [{"key": "tags", "match": {"any": ["alert", "cve"]}}]}

#### Range filter (integer/datetime)
  {"must": [{"key": "severity", "range": {"gte": 3, "lte": 5}}]}

#### Compound (AND)
  {"must": [
    {"key": "project", "match": {"value": "sandfly"}},
    {"key": "severity", "range": {"gte": 4}}
  ]}

#### Compound (OR)
  {"should": [
    {"key": "tags", "match": {"value": "cve"}},
    {"key": "tags", "match": {"value": "alert"}}
  ]}

#### Exclude (NOT)
  {"must_not": [{"key": "status", "match": {"value": "resolved"}}]}

#### Null check
  {"must": [{"key": "resolved_at", "is_null": true}]}

