## DEPLOYMENT TOPOLOGY

### Docker Compose (current — homelab)
  aiana-qdrant runs as container in the AIANA Docker stack.
  Persistent volume mounted at /qdrant/storage inside container.
  Data survives container restart; does NOT survive docker compose down -v.

### k3s StatefulSet (target)
  For production resilience, Qdrant should run as a StatefulSet:
  - PVC backed by local-path StorageClass (node-local — must use nodeSelector)
  - Or longhorn StorageClass for cross-node replication
  - ⚠ local-path PVs are node-local — if pod reschedules to different node,
    data is gone. Use nodeSelector to pin Qdrant pod to its storage node.
  - Expose via ClusterIP Service (internal) or NodePort (for external homelab access)

### Per-fabric isolated instances (planned)
  Pattern: each fabric that needs semantic memory gets its own Qdrant.
  qdrant-fabric MCP server target: a different QDRANT_URL per fabric context.
  No cross-contamination of vector spaces across fabric domains.

