## FABRIC-SDK OSI MAPPING

qdrant-fabric lives at L3 (Network / Gateway) and L6 (Presentation / MCP):

  L6 (MCP)         — qdrant-fabric IS an MCP server. Its tool contract is L6.
                     Claude calls qdrant-fabric tools at L6 exactly like any other
                     MCP server in the fabric-sdk stack.

  L3 (Gateway)     — Vector storage is the knowledge plane of the F-RIB.
                     Every fabric's Qdrant collection is a knowledge store that
                     feeds the gateway's routing decisions. AIANA reads from
                     aiana-qdrant to answer recall queries. The gateway uses AIANA
                     recall to determine which fabric has the best context for a query.
                     qdrant-fabric is the ops interface to that knowledge infrastructure.

  Relationship to AIANA (L5):
    AIANA is the semantic memory LAYER — it knows what the vectors mean.
    qdrant-fabric is the PLUMBING — it stores and retrieves vectors without interpretation.
    AIANA uses qdrant-fabric's underlying instances but has its own abstraction above it.
    qdrant-fabric operates the Qdrant instances that AIANA depends on.
    When AIANA's vector indexing is broken → qdrant-fabric diagnoses the symptom,
    aiana-ops diagnoses the cause, both coordinate on the fix.

  The foundry metaphor:
    Every MCP server in the stack — UniFi, Proxmox, Sandfly, git-steer, n8n-fabric —
    produces knowledge (operational events, decisions, alerts, audit logs).
    That knowledge flows into Qdrant via AIANA's ingestion pipeline.
    qdrant-fabric is the interface to the foundry itself.
    The 229+ AIANA memories, n8n workflow indexes, Sandfly security docs —
    that's not just data. That's the training ground for local LLM inference.
    Without qdrant-fabric, the foundry has no operator.
